Ok, I have another question (sorry - this should be my last one!). The function I'm using involves a LogSumExp calculation (in other words, adding up a bunch of exponentials and taking the log of that sum). With large numbers I run into some nasty numerical issues (e.g., infinite values), so this is necessary. The calculation involves taking the maximum value of the series (see here <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LogSumExp#log-sum-exp_trick_for_log-domain_calculations>), but the LogSumExp(x1, x2, ..., xn) function is technically differentiable even with this max. The values in the series are a linear combination of data and parameters (like a regression), so obviously this non-differentiable "max" function depends on the parameters. If I use the "max" function built into TMB "Type" vectors, would this be OK?

Peter

